On Sat, 10 Oct 2026 08:58:32 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> just task in the mail branch that iterates over each added email file in
> @, and makes a new commit with just: prefix followed by the email
> subject name.

Posted as "[PATCH] mail: Add just commit-mail" [1], against the mail
branch (base-commit is mail@upstream). It takes each file added under
maildir/ in @ and makes one commit per file, named for the Subject
header. Folded subjects are joined onto one line.

On the prefix: I defaulted to "mail: " rather than "just: ". Every
message commit on the mail branch uses it, including your own
"mail: just: commit-mail", so I read "just:" as the area of your
subject. If you did want "just: ", it is an argument:

    just commit-mail 'just: '

or a one-word change to the default. Tell me which and I'll revise.

> It should only commit files that have been added, not moved, edited,
> etc.

It picks files by jj's diff status, so only "added" counts. Renames
(new/ -> cur/, flag changes, archive moves) and edits stay in @, as
do added files outside maildir/. I tested this in a scratch repo
with a mix of added, renamed, and edited mail.

